%N A399646 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} O(2*k)/(k*(2*k+1)), where O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind).
%H A399646 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://euro.ecom.cmu.edu/people/faculty/mshamos/cat.pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2007. See p. 463.
%H A399646 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 13.
%H A399646 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399646 Equals log(2) + Pi/2 - 3*zeta(2)/4 = A002162 + A019669 + A111003 (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019).
%F A399646 Equals 2 * Integral_{x>=1} arctan(x)^2/x^3 dx (Shamos, 2007).
%e A399646 1.030242957218672101294242438113409118259872408142709...
%t A399646 RealDigits[Log[2] + Pi/2 - 3*Zeta[2]/4, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A399646 (PARI) log(2) + Pi/2 - 3*zeta(2)/4
%Y A399646 Cf. A350669, A350670.
%Y A399646 Cf. A002162, A013661, A019669, A111003, A399649.
%Y A399646 Cf. A072691 (Sum_{k>=1} O(k)/(k*(2k+1))), A253191 ((1/2)*Sum_{k>=1} H(k)/(k*(2k+1))), A399647 (Sum_{k>=1} H(2*k)/(k*(2k+1))).
